From: OpenHarmony PC Adaptation <noreply@openharmony.io>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 16:01:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] llvm: classify HarmonyOS as a Unix-like platform

Handle CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME=HarmonyOS in LLVM's Unix-like option branch so the
standard LLVM_ON_UNIX settings are selected on OHOS.

Origin: https://github.com/root-project/llvm-project/tree/cling-llvm20-20260119-01
Upstream-Status: Not-Submitted [contest adaptation]
Source-Commit: 6fb92ab985353ed71faec49beaaf5d111e041f8c
Modification-Layer: 1 (CMake module source)
Knowledge-Ref: E140
---
 llvm/cmake/modules/HandleLLVMOptions.cmake | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/llvm/cmake/modules/HandleLLVMOptions.cmake b/llvm/cmake/modules/HandleLLVMOptions.cmake
--- a/llvm/cmake/modules/HandleLLVMOptions.cmake
+++ b/llvm/cmake/modules/HandleLLVMOptions.cmake
@@ -219,7 +219,7 @@ if(WIN32)
     set(LLVM_ON_WIN32 1)
     set(LLVM_ON_UNIX 0)
   endif(CYGWIN)
-elseif(FUCHSIA OR UNIX)
+elseif(FUCHSIA OR UNIX OR CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "^(OHOS|HarmonyOS)$")
   set(LLVM_ON_WIN32 0)
   set(LLVM_ON_UNIX 1)
   if(APPLE OR ${CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME} MATCHES "AIX")
--
2.45.2
